# Cumulative mechanical motor-shaft position for ESC telemetry and odometry.
#
# This is an optional complement to Status and StatusExtended; it does not
# replace either existing message. The source may use Hall sensors, encoders,
# or sensorless position estimation, but shall indicate invalid measurements.
#
# A positive increment denotes forward rotation according to RPMCommand.
# esc_index follows Status/StatusExtended indexing (zero is the first ESC).
#
# valid is false when position continuity/measurement is unavailable. Receivers
# must not integrate a transition across invalid data without re-establishing
# a position origin and verifying a plausible increment.
#
# origin_toggle changes state whenever the position counter is re-zeroed or
# its origin or scaling changes. It is a persistent parity bit, not a pulse.
# Receivers must re-baseline when it changes, and also when a node restarts,
# whenever a gap prevents continuity from being established, or when the
# reported delta is physically implausible. Two or more origin changes between
# observed samples cannot be identified reliably using one bit alone.
#
# In integer mode, ticks_per_revolution must be greater than zero; position
# ticks wrap modulo 2^32. In float mode, revolutions is a finite signed value.
# Neither representation implies a wheel transmission ratio or a wheel size.
#
# Frame size: tick mode 56 bits (7 bytes), float mode 40 bits (5 bytes).
# DTID 1037 is provisional until accepted by the DroneCAN maintainers.

uint5 esc_index
bool valid
bool origin_toggle
MotorPositionValue position
